ck", 90.416, 90.759], ["b", 91.021, 91.426], ["keep", 91.579, 91.799], ["all", 91.799, 92.142], ["nine", 92.142, 92.441], ["thousand", 92.441, 93.004], ["follow", 93.204, 93.652], ["if", 93.652, 93.732], ["you", 93.732, 93.846], ["wouldn't", 93.846, 94.066], ["have", 94.066, 94.189], ["run", 94.189, 94.541]], "lines": [[0.0, 4.828, "In this town, wars are fought by war beasts, and the winner keeps the loser's crown."], [5.099, 9.604, "This morning, the enemy's war stag knelt to me. So their king woke up a mountain."], [9.834, 13.95, "It was his first war beast, and its antlers held nine thousand crowns."], [14.246, 16.799, "My stag stepped in front of me. I walked around him."], [17.04, 21.388, "The mountain raised one hoof over my head. Their whole army ran. I didn't."], [21.585, 24.359, "The hoof stopped. Then the mountain knelt. To me."], [24.574, 27.96, "Nine thousand crowns came down around me like golden hail."], [28.173, 31.955, "The king screamed, \"Get up! Crush him!\" The mountain didn't move."], [32.179, 35.943, "So I looked up at the king and said, \"Your turn. Come stand where I'm standing.\""], [36.212, 41.69, "He wouldn't come out from behind his wall. In nine thousand wars, he had never once stood in front of a beast."], [41.913, 48.268, "That's when I understood. A war beast only kneels to its true king, and a true king is just the one who doesn't run."], [48.54, 54.412, "The mountain laid its neck down like a road, and I walked up. From the top, I could see every town he ever took."], [54.653, 59.077, "\"You're a kid with a goat,\" the king yelled. \"You can't rule nine thousand towns!\""], [59.349, 60.8, "He was right. So I didn't."], [61.038, 65.48, "The winner keeps the loser's crown. I won. That made them mine to give back."], [65.689, 68.979, "The two stags carried them home, one crown to every town."], [69.197, 75.319, "By sunset, every town had come to take its throne back. They pulled the king's castle apart, one chair at a time."], [75.554, 78.949, "The king was left standing in an empty field, with nowhere to sit."], [79.209, 83.918, "A crown you take makes a town afraid of you. A crown you give back makes it follow you."], [84.16, 87.872, "I kept one crown. Our goat wears it. He thinks he won the war."], [88.124, 93.004, "Would you have given them back? A, give them back. B, keep all nine thousand."], [93.204, 94.541, "Follow if you wouldn't have run."]]}